OL,3,GNEWSABritish baseball champions crowned
OL,4,Aa century after win
OL,5,
OL,6,FIt's America's national pastime, but
OL,7,Fduring the 1920s it was a small town in
OL,8,Fthe Cotswolds that was flying the flag
OL,9,Ffor baseball in the UK.
OL,11,FAt the same time Babe Ruth was leading
OL,12,Fthe New York Yankees to the top of the
OL,13,Fsport across the pond, Chipping Norton
OL,14,Fwere being crowned British champions in
OL,15,Fback-to-back years.
OL,17,FBut in a wait that's taken longer than
OL,18,Fthe Red Sox needed to break the Curse
OL,19,Fof the Bambino, the Cotswold market
OL,20,Ftown's success had never been
OL,21,Fofficially recognised.
OL,23,APub: 01-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB S Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
FL,340,330,200,160,0,100
